./noemaforge/docs/quality/BRANCH_RECONCILIATION_0.32.2.md:15:| `v0.32.1-prelaunch` | ahead of `main` by 3 commits | canonical 0.32.2 base | Use as the functional base for 0.32.2. |
./noemaforge/docs/quality/BRANCH_RECONCILIATION_0.32.2.md:16:| `release/0.32.2-hardening` | ahead of `main` by 17 commits | ahead of `v0.32.1-prelaunch` by 14 commits, behind by 0 | Continue as 0.32.2 hardening branch. |
./noemaforge/docs/quality/BRANCH_RECONCILIATION_0.32.2.md:20:`release/0.32.2-hardening` is already based on `v0.32.1-prelaunch`; it is ahead by 14 commits and behind by 0. This means the latest prelaunch branch content is included by ancestry, not by a partial cherry-pick.
./noemaforge/docs/quality/BRANCH_RECONCILIATION_0.32.2.md:22:`v0.32.1-prelaunch` is ahead of `v0.32.0-alpha` by 1 commit and behind by 0. Therefore `v0.32.0-alpha` is included by ancestry.
./noemaforge/docs/quality/BRANCH_RECONCILIATION_0.32.2.md:24:`v0.32.1-prelaunch` is ahead of `v0.32.0` by 2 commits and behind by 0. Therefore `v0.32.0` is included by ancestry.
./noemaforge/docs/quality/BRANCH_RECONCILIATION_0.32.2.md:30:1. Preserve `v0.32.1-prelaunch` as the content base unless there is an explicit 0.32.2 safety reason to change it.
./noemaforge/docs/quality/BRANCH_RECONCILIATION_0.32.2.md:40:The following broad change groups are already included from earlier branches because the 0.32.2 branch descends from `v0.32.1-prelaunch`:
./noemaforge/docs/quality/BRANCH_RECONCILIATION_0.32.2.md:47:- manifest/checksum material from 0.32.1 prelaunch.
./noemaforge/docs/quality/BRANCH_RECONCILIATION_0.32.2.md:63:The draft PR targets `main`, while the functional release branch is based on `v0.32.1-prelaunch`. This is expected but makes review noisy: GitHub shows the whole 0.32.1 prelaunch import plus 0.32.2 hardening. For review, compare `v0.32.1-prelaunch...release/0.32.2-hardening`.
./noemaforge/docs/quality/BRANCH_RECONCILIATION_0.32.2.md:67:The compare from `main` shows `LICENSE` removed by the 0.32.1 branch history. This should be reviewed before final merge. Recommended default: restore or preserve the license file unless there is an explicit legal/product reason not to.
./noemaforge/docs/quality/BRANCH_RECONCILIATION_0.32.2.md:71:Earlier branches contain many historical install scripts and versioned wiki files. `v0.32.1-prelaunch` already made a cleanup decision. Do not re-add older scripts unless they are moved under a clearly historical path.
./noemaforge/docs/quality/BRANCH_RECONCILIATION_0.32.2.md:75:The repository branch inventory does not expose only three divergent files. The practical branch graph is larger: `v0.32.1-prelaunch` supersedes `v0.32.0` and `v0.32.0-alpha`, while `Verion-32.0` is identical to `main`. If there are three specific external branched files, they must be uploaded or identified by path/branch.
./noemaforge/docs/quality/BRANCH_RECONCILIATION_0.32.2.md:79:Use `v0.32.1-prelaunch` as the canonical content baseline and continue applying 0.32.2 hardening commits on top of it. Do not cherry-pick from `v0.32.0`, `v0.32.0-alpha` or `Verion-32.0` because those branches are either already included or contain no unique content.
./noemaforge/docs/quality/BRANCH_RECONCILIATION_0.32.2.md:83:- [ ] Replace remaining Python hardcoded `RUNTIME_VERSION = ...` assignments with `from noemaforge_version import RUNTIME_VERSION`.
./noemaforge/docs/quality/BRANCH_RECONCILIATION_0.32.2.md:93:Continue development in `release/0.32.2-hardening`, but review diffs against `v0.32.1-prelaunch`, not against `main`, until the final merge-to-main step.
