./noemaforge/docs/reference/PROJECT_CONTEXT.md:3:NoemaForge is being prepared as a local-first `0.32.1` prelaunch package. The active package root is `noemaforge/`; runtime contracts live in `noemaforge/src`, deterministic policies live in `noemaforge/configs`, and executable coverage lives in `noemaforge/tests`.
./noemaforge/docs/reference/PROJECT_CONTEXT.md:33:Installed pipeline CLI wiring is now covered by an offline installer contract. `pipeline-cli-install-wiring-core` validates that the promoted installer copies the package payload before public command links, exposes `/usr/local/bin/noemaforge` as a symlink to `/opt/noemaforge/bin/noemaforge`, prints that link in dry-run mode, and keeps setup selftest coverage for `noemaforge/bin/noemaforge`. The packaged CLI must resolve its canonical self under `$ROOT/bin/noemaforge`, reject public wrapper paths as canonical self, dispatch `noemaforge pipeline` to `src/pipeline_runtime.py`, and keep the expected pipeline subcommands visible through the installed entrypoint. Closed by `pipeline-cli-install-wiring-core`.
./noemaforge/docs/reference/PROJECT_CONTEXT.md:51:Target ToolProxy capability issue/verify smoke now has its own open evidence contract. `toolproxy-capability-live-smoke-readiness-core` records `blocked_until_target_toolproxy_capability_live_smoke_evidence`, requires target ToolProxy service/socket baseline, operator approval scoped to issue/verify, live capability issue, live capability verify, token revocation with redacted evidence and a hashed forensics archive. The local validator checks policy, example, registry and documentation shape only; it does not run ToolProxy, systemd, socket, revoke or archive commands.
./noemaforge/docs/reference/PROJECT_CONTEXT.md:53:Target ToolProxy socket plus `llm.chat` smoke is also separated from the broad target-live gate. `toolproxy-live-llm-smoke-readiness-core` records `blocked_until_target_toolproxy_live_llm_smoke_evidence`, requires target ToolProxy service/socket baseline, operator approval scoped to live LLM smoke, `llm.chat` capability binding, live `noemaforge toolproxy smoke --live-llm --json` output, model identity, token revocation with redacted evidence and a hashed forensics archive. The local validator checks policy, example, registry and documentation shape only; it does not run ToolProxy, systemd, socket, LLM, revoke or archive commands.
./noemaforge/docs/reference/PROJECT_CONTEXT.md:87:The default model-runtime policy is now an executable decision instead of an open product question. `default-model-runtime-policy-core` selects `cpu_safe_always_on_with_gpu_on_demand`: NoemaForge defaults to a CPU-safe runtime posture, keeps GPU work explicit and staged through the existing device-policy boundary, preserves one active heavy worker and does not enable boot-time LLM autostart. The policy is validated against `runtime-device-policy.json`, model profiles, runtime default safety, device-policy staging and the Admin GUI fallback state.
./noemaforge/docs/reference/PROJECT_CONTEXT.md:93:Production GUI install is now a composed offline readiness contract rather than a single unchecked shell script. `production-gui-installer-core` ties together root `setup.sh`, the promoted installer, package dry-run validation, setup front-door/mode contracts, stateful Admin GUI assets, timer-driven GUI systemd units, boot-mode CLI controls and recovery helpers. Production GUI installer boundary: dry-run and selftest are the first path, live host install is root-gated, GUI autostart is timer-driven, Admin GUI starts without hidden LLM autostart, and live target validation remains a separate hardware-dependent gate.
./noemaforge/docs/reference/PROJECT_CONTEXT.md:97:The patched10 full-composite real run also has an executable readiness contract now. `full-composite-target-run-readiness-core` records `blocked_until_target_full_composite_evidence`, requires patched10 install baseline evidence, target preflight, operator-approved `--full_composite 0` command plan, a run transcript with TTY status, first-start summary artifacts, display/abort recovery evidence and a forensics archive. The validator stays offline and does not run `first-start`, systemd, GUI recovery or forensics commands; the target run TODO remains open until the NoemaForge host produces and archives those artifacts.
./noemaforge/docs/reference/PROJECT_CONTEXT.md:101:The `/run/nologin` recovery confirmation is now its own target-evidence contract. `nologin-recovery-readiness-core` records `blocked_until_target_nologin_recovery_evidence`, requires pre-recovery nologin and display baseline, operator-approved abort cleanup, post-recovery `/run/nologin` absence, display-manager or GDM active state and a forensics archive. Local validation stays offline and cannot run systemd, recovery or forensics commands.
./noemaforge/docs/reference/PROJECT_CONTEXT.md:103:The Debian Trixie emergency GUI recovery validation is also explicit but remains target-machine-only. `emergency-gui-recovery-readiness-core` records `blocked_until_target_emergency_gui_recovery_evidence`, requires display-manager and GDM baseline evidence, operator-approved `sudo noemaforge pause --wait` and `sudo noemaforge gui-rescue --wait` transcripts, display-manager alias-to-GDM evidence, post-rescue `/run/nologin` absence and a reviewed forensics archive. The local validator checks only policy, example, registry and docs shape; it does not call systemd, recovery or archive commands.
./noemaforge/docs/reference/PROJECT_CONTEXT.md:105:The share automount reboot guard is also explicit and target-only. `share-automount-reboot-readiness-core` records `blocked_until_target_share_reboot_evidence`, requires fstab and automount unit evidence for `/mnt/noemaforge-share`, operator-approved reboot evidence, post-reboot emergency and rescue target state, post-reboot share access and a forensics archive. The local validator only checks policy, registry, docs and evidence shape; it does not reboot, mount shares or query systemd.
./noemaforge/docs/reference/PROJECT_CONTEXT.md:107:The post-reboot validation archive is now explicit as the next target-only evidence bundle. `post-reboot-validation-archive-readiness-core` records `blocked_until_target_post_reboot_archive_evidence`, requires post-reboot boot ID and failed-unit evidence, gateway/main-backend/display-manager service state, operator-approved live smoke transcripts, forensics and journal archive hashes, and a wiki patch bundle manifest that references the target evidence. The local validator only checks policy, registry, docs and example shape; it does not run systemd, journal, forensics, live smoke or wiki patch commands.
./noemaforge/docs/reference/PROJECT_CONTEXT.md:109:The post-reboot service health check is now split out from the broader archive gate. `post-reboot-service-health-readiness-core` records `blocked_until_target_post_reboot_service_health_evidence`, requires the target boot ID and system-running state, gateway service health, operator-approved manual `noemaforge-llama@main` start/stop evidence, ToolProxy service health, gateway/ToolProxy socket or API smoke output and a reviewed archive hash. The local validator checks only policy, example, registry and documentation shape; it does not run systemd, socket probes or LLM commands.
./noemaforge/docs/reference/PROJECT_CONTEXT.md:111:The composite post-reboot GPU/GDM/gateway/ToolProxy line is now an executable target-evidence contract instead of a broad reminder. `post-reboot-gpu-gdm-gateway-toolproxy-readiness-core` records `blocked_until_target_post_reboot_gpu_gdm_gateway_toolproxy_evidence`, requires boot baseline, operator approval, display-manager/GDM state, NVIDIA signal, gateway and ToolProxy service state, gateway and ToolProxy socket smoke evidence, redaction review and a hashed archive. The local validator checks only policy, example, registry and documentation shape; it does not run systemd, NVIDIA, gateway, ToolProxy, LLM or archive commands.
./noemaforge/docs/reference/PROJECT_CONTEXT.md:113:The gateway plus main-backend live smoke is now narrowed as its own target-evidence contract. `gateway-main-live-smoke-readiness-core` records `blocked_until_target_gateway_main_live_smoke_evidence`, requires gateway and `noemaforge-llama@main` service/socket baseline, operator approval, manual main-backend start evidence, gateway socket/status evidence, gateway smoke and chat transcripts, backend stop evidence and a reviewed archive hash. The local validator checks only policy, example, registry and documentation shape; it does not run systemd, socket probes, gateway commands or LLM commands.
./noemaforge/docs/reference/PROJECT_CONTEXT.md:115:The Debian Trixie preflight run is now an explicit target-evidence contract instead of an implied operator note. `trixie-preflight-target-readiness-core` records `blocked_until_target_trixie_preflight_evidence`, requires operator approval for the read-only `sudo noemaforge trixie-preflight --json` command, JSON parse evidence, Debian/kernel baseline, dependency surface, runtime socket snapshot and archive hash. The local validator checks only policy, example, registry and documentation shape; it does not run sudo, preflight, systemd, socket probes or remediation commands.
./noemaforge/docs/reference/PROJECT_CONTEXT.md:117:Post-failure support capture is also explicit. `failure-forensics-bundle-readiness-core` records `blocked_until_target_failure_forensics_bundle_evidence`, requires a target failure timestamp and surface, operator approval for `sudo noemaforge forensics --dry-run` and `sudo noemaforge forensics`, bundle path, SHA256 and file inventory, redaction evidence for secrets, model weights, Vault content, browser profiles and token paths, runtime log coverage and a reviewed findings/follow-up record. The local validator checks only policy, example, registry and documentation shape; it does not run sudo, forensics, journal, systemd or upload commands.
./noemaforge/docs/reference/PROJECT_CONTEXT.md:119:The target-hardware GUI recovery path now has a separate evidence contract from the broader emergency GUI recovery slice. `target-gui-recovery-path-readiness-core` records `blocked_until_target_gui_recovery_path_evidence`, requires pre-recovery display-manager/GDM and graphical target state, operator-approved `sudo noemaforge pause --wait`, operator-approved `sudo noemaforge gui-rescue --wait`, proof that pause preceded rescue, post-rescue display state, `/run/nologin` absence, a forensics archive hash and inspected follow-up notes. The local validator checks only policy, example, registry and documentation shape; it does not run sudo, recovery, systemd or archive commands.
./noemaforge/docs/reference/PROJECT_CONTEXT.md:121:The systemd/GDM/NVIDIA live-validation line is now narrowed from the broader target-live gate. `systemd-gdm-nvidia-live-validation-readiness-core` records `blocked_until_target_systemd_gdm_nvidia_live_validation_evidence`, requires boot ID, system-running and failed-unit state, operator approval, display-manager/GDM and graphical target state, NVIDIA driver/device/module evidence, secure-boot and kernel driver log evidence, `/run/nologin` and seat recovery guards, and a reviewed archive hash. The local validator checks only policy, example, registry and documentation shape; it does not run systemd, GDM, NVIDIA, journal, loginctl or archive commands.
./noemaforge/docs/reference/PROJECT_CONTEXT.md:127:The local dashboard launcher also owns the user-level dashboard autostart boundary. `dashboard-launcher-core` now validates `autostart-enable`, `autostart-disable` and `autostart-status` as operator-scoped systemd user timer commands under `XDG_CONFIG_HOME`, with dry-run output, no root requirement and no hidden LLM or media backend startup.
./noemaforge/docs/reference/PROJECT_CONTEXT.md:157:No happy-path install or boot-mode flow requires hand-editing systemd units
