./noemaforge/docs/README.md:3:This documentation tree was consolidated for NoemaForge `0.32.1`.
./noemaforge/docs/README.md:50:- `noemaforge/configs/noemaforge.runtime.yaml` and `noemaforge/src/multios_runtime_contract.py` enforce the MultiOS runtime host split with Linux systemd preserved, Windows/macOS control-only paths and remote HTTP disabled by default.
./noemaforge/docs/README.md:75:- `toolproxy-live-llm-smoke-readiness-core` is enforced by `noemaforge/configs/toolproxy-live-llm-smoke-readiness-policy.json` and `noemaforge/src/toolproxy_live_llm_smoke_readiness_runtime.py` for target-machine ToolProxy socket plus `llm.chat` smoke; it keeps the item in `blocked_until_target_toolproxy_live_llm_smoke_evidence`, requires ToolProxy service/socket baseline, operator approval, `llm.chat` capability binding, live LLM smoke JSON, token revocation and archive evidence, and never runs ToolProxy, systemd, socket or LLM commands locally.
./noemaforge/docs/README.md:76:- `gateway-main-live-smoke-readiness-core` is enforced by `noemaforge/configs/gateway-main-live-smoke-readiness-policy.json` and `noemaforge/src/gateway_main_live_smoke_readiness_runtime.py` for target-machine gateway plus `noemaforge-llama@main` smoke; it keeps the item in `blocked_until_target_gateway_main_live_smoke_evidence`, requires service baseline, operator approval, manual main-backend start, gateway socket/status evidence, gateway smoke/chat transcript and backend stop/archive evidence, and never runs systemd, gateway, socket or LLM commands locally.
./noemaforge/docs/README.md:79:- `production-gui-installer-core` is enforced by `noemaforge/configs/production-gui-installer-policy.json` and `noemaforge/src/production_gui_installer_runtime.py`. Production GUI installer boundary: root `setup.sh`, the promoted installer, delayed GUI systemd timer, Admin GUI dashboard assets, boot-mode CLI, recovery helpers and dry-run/root guards are validated together before any live host install.
./noemaforge/docs/README.md:84:- `emergency-gui-recovery-readiness-core` is enforced by `noemaforge/configs/emergency-gui-recovery-readiness-policy.json` and `noemaforge/src/emergency_gui_recovery_readiness_runtime.py` for the patched10 Debian Trixie emergency GUI recovery check: it keeps the item in `blocked_until_target_emergency_gui_recovery_evidence`, requires display-manager/GDM baseline, operator-approved `pause --wait` and `gui-rescue --wait`, display-manager alias evidence, post-rescue `/run/nologin` guard and a forensics archive, and never runs live systemd or recovery commands locally.
./noemaforge/docs/README.md:87:- `post-reboot-service-health-readiness-core` is enforced by `noemaforge/configs/post-reboot-service-health-readiness-policy.json` and `noemaforge/src/post_reboot_service_health_readiness_runtime.py` for the target post-reboot health check of gateway, ToolProxy and `noemaforge-llama@main`: it keeps the item in `blocked_until_target_post_reboot_service_health_evidence`, requires boot baseline, gateway service state, operator-approved manual main-backend start/stop state, ToolProxy service state, socket/API smoke output and archive evidence, and never runs systemd, socket or LLM commands locally.
./noemaforge/docs/README.md:88:- `post-reboot-gpu-gdm-gateway-toolproxy-readiness-core` is enforced by `noemaforge/configs/post-reboot-gpu-gdm-gateway-toolproxy-readiness-policy.json` and `noemaforge/src/post_reboot_gpu_gdm_gateway_toolproxy_readiness_runtime.py` for the composite target-machine post-reboot GPU/GDM/gateway/ToolProxy validation: it keeps the item in `blocked_until_target_post_reboot_gpu_gdm_gateway_toolproxy_evidence`, requires boot baseline, operator approval, GPU/GDM state, gateway and ToolProxy service state, gateway and ToolProxy socket smoke evidence, archive hash and redaction review, and never runs systemd, NVIDIA, gateway, ToolProxy, LLM or archive commands locally.
./noemaforge/docs/README.md:89:- `trixie-preflight-target-readiness-core` is enforced by `noemaforge/configs/trixie-preflight-target-readiness-policy.json` and `noemaforge/src/trixie_preflight_target_readiness_runtime.py` for the target `sudo noemaforge trixie-preflight --json` run: it keeps the item in `blocked_until_target_trixie_preflight_evidence`, requires operator-approved read-only preflight JSON, Debian/kernel baseline, dependency surface, runtime socket snapshot and archive evidence, and never runs sudo, preflight, systemd or socket commands locally.
./noemaforge/docs/README.md:90:- `failure-forensics-bundle-readiness-core` is enforced by `noemaforge/configs/failure-forensics-bundle-readiness-policy.json` and `noemaforge/src/failure_forensics_bundle_readiness_runtime.py` for post-failure `sudo noemaforge forensics` capture: it keeps the item in `blocked_until_target_failure_forensics_bundle_evidence`, requires failure context, operator-approved dry-run and real forensics transcripts, bundle path/hash/file inventory, redaction review, runtime log coverage and inspected follow-up routing, and never runs sudo, forensics, journal, systemd or upload commands locally.
./noemaforge/docs/README.md:91:- `target-gui-recovery-path-readiness-core` is enforced by `noemaforge/configs/target-gui-recovery-path-readiness-policy.json` and `noemaforge/src/target_gui_recovery_path_readiness_runtime.py` for target-hardware GUI recovery: it keeps the item in `blocked_until_target_gui_recovery_path_evidence`, requires display/GDM baseline, operator-approved `pause --wait`, operator-approved `gui-rescue --wait`, post-rescue display and `/run/nologin` state, forensics archive and inspection follow-up evidence, and never runs sudo, recovery, systemd or archive commands locally.
./noemaforge/docs/README.md:92:- `systemd-gdm-nvidia-live-validation-readiness-core` is enforced by `noemaforge/configs/systemd-gdm-nvidia-live-validation-readiness-policy.json` and `noemaforge/src/systemd_gdm_nvidia_live_validation_readiness_runtime.py` for target-machine systemd, GDM/display-manager and NVIDIA validation: it keeps the item in `blocked_until_target_systemd_gdm_nvidia_live_validation_evidence`, requires boot/systemd baseline, operator approval, display-manager/GDM state, NVIDIA driver/device signal, secure-boot/kernel log evidence, post-reboot recovery guards and archive evidence, and never runs systemd, GDM, NVIDIA, journal, loginctl or archive commands locally.
./noemaforge/docs/README.md:93:- `noemaforge/configs/dashboard-launcher-policy.json` and `noemaforge/src/dashboard_launcher_runtime.py` enforce the local dashboard launcher commands, operator-writable dashboard-state output, static UI serving, user-level dashboard autostart enable/disable/status controls and no LLM/media autostart.
./noemaforge/docs/README.md:106:- `pipeline-cli-install-wiring-core` is enforced by `noemaforge/configs/pipeline-cli-install-wiring-policy.json`, `noemaforge/contracts/pipeline_cli_install_wiring.schema.json` and `noemaforge/src/pipeline_cli_install_wiring_runtime.py`: the installer contract verifies `/usr/local/bin/noemaforge` is a dry-run-visible symlink to `/opt/noemaforge/bin/noemaforge`, setup selftest parses the packaged CLI, and the installed public entrypoint exposes the pipeline command surface. Closed by `pipeline-cli-install-wiring-core`.
./noemaforge/docs/README.md:134:- `runtime-default-safety-core` is enforced by `noemaforge/configs/runtime-default-safety-policy.json` and `noemaforge/src/runtime_default_safety_runtime.py` for `max_active_llms=1`, manual-only heavy LLM boot, GUI `runtime_only`, woGUI CPU bootstrap and sequential team-member defaults.
./noemaforge/docs/README.md:136:- `systemd-happy-path-core` is enforced by `noemaforge/configs/systemd-happy-path-policy.json` and `noemaforge/src/systemd_happy_path_runtime.py`: No happy-path install or boot-mode flow requires hand-editing systemd units; use `noemaforge boot-mode` / setup wrappers and dry-run commands instead.
