{"body":"## Mission\n\nUse Codex to drive the 0.33.0 prod-ready loop from the currently observed install/re-entry findings through fixes, documentation, automated recheck, requirements reconciliation, and TODO execution.\n\nThis is the umbrella task for the current NF 0.33.0 hardening pass.\n\n## Primary branch / target\n\n- Work from the current release line: `release/0.33.0-dev` unless repository policy says otherwise.\n- Keep changes small enough to review, but do not stop after only one local fix if adjacent issues are part of the same release/install surface.\n- Prefer one coherent PR for closely related install/re-entry hardening, or multiple PRs if reviewability requires it.\n\n## Current confirmed issues to resolve first\n\n### Install / post-install / re-entry process\n\n- #212 — installed payload loses executable bits for smoke/preflight/operator scripts.\n- #213 — installer installs `/opt/noemaforge` as invoking user and group-writable instead of root-owned runtime payload.\n- #214 — post-install smoke should be profile-aware; `runtime_only` should not fail on intentionally missing main backend.\n- #215 — `safe-start runtime_only` mutates persistent systemd enablement despite manual boot mode.\n- #216 — installed systemd units rely on hotfix drop-ins and stale 0.32.1 unit metadata.\n- #217 — post-install `mvp-smoke` reports failures without actionable stderr/artifact links.\n\n### App/config blockers found during re-entry\n\n- #218 — pipeline catalog validation fails because media/admin pipelines reference missing `media_team`.\n- #219 — `mvp-smoke` pipeline lifecycle check is blocked by `degraded_readonly` under `degraded_selected` staffing.\n- #220 — CLI consistency: `pipeline validate` emits validation JSON but rejects `--json`.\n\n## Required behavior for Codex loop\n\n### 1. Solve all relevant open issues before adding new scope\n\nStart with the above issue set. For each issue:\n\n- identify the source files responsible;\n- implement the smallest robust production fix;\n- add or update tests;\n- update release manifests/checksums if this repository requires it;\n- preserve the Trixie safety invariant: no heavy LLM autostart, max active LLMs = 1, `runtime_only` means gateway/toolproxy only.\n\n### 2. Token/rate-limit behavior\n\nIf Codex hits usage, rate, or token limits:\n\n- do not keep retrying in a tight loop;\n- parse or infer the reset time when available;\n- write/update the existing runner pause marker if used by the project, e.g. `runner-pause-until.txt` under the configured Codex home/workflow location;\n- resume automatically when the reset time passes;\n- leave a compact status note with what was completed, what is pending, and the next command/action.\n\n### 3. Documentation phase\n\nWhen the relevant issues are fixed and tests are green, update documentation before declaring done:\n\n- install/re-entry docs;\n- Trixie/secure boot/NVIDIA notes if referenced by the flow;\n- operator commands for `runtime_only`, `bootstrap_cpu_llm`, and post-install smoke;\n- manual boot-mode semantics;\n- expected degraded-mode behavior;\n- troubleshooting docs for `mvp-smoke` and pipeline validation.\n\nAvoid dumping research logs into docs. Convert findings into concise, stable operator guidance.\n\n### 4. Automated recheck loop\n\nAfter docs are updated, run the appropriate automated verification:\n\n- source/unit tests relevant to the changed files;\n- CLI validation tests;\n- catalog validation;\n- post-install/install-layout checks if available;\n- `noemaforge pipeline validate` / `noemaforge pipeline validate --json` once implemented;\n- `noemaforge mvp-smoke --json` or its test equivalent;\n- profile-aware smoke for `runtime_only`.\n\nFor every newly found problem that is not fixed in the same pass:\n\n- create a GitHub issue with evidence and reproduction steps;\n- link it from the current PR/umbrella issue;\n- then return to issue-solving mode.\n\n### 5. Requirements reconciliation\n\nAfter recheck and fixes, compare the current implementation against the original/current 0.33.0 requirements:\n\n- what is implemented;\n- what is partially implemented;\n- what is missing;\n- what is intentionally deferred;\n- what has changed due to runtime/safety constraints.\n\nConvert gaps into new TODO points. Separate:\n\n- 0.33.0 release-blocking TODOs;\n- post-0.33.0 TODOs;\n- research/design TODOs;\n- target-host-only/manual validation TODOs.\n\n### 6. TODO execution order\n\nAfter requirements reconciliation:\n\n1. solve 0.33.0 TODO points first;\n2. then solve remaining non-0.33.0 TODO points by priority;\n3. keep each PR bounded and test-backed;\n4. never silently change boot persistence, heavy LLM autostart policy, or writable runtime paths.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\nThis umbrella task is done only when:\n\n- #212-#220 are fixed or explicitly closed with a documented reason;\n- clean install/re-entry produces correct `/opt/noemaforge` ownership and executable modes;\n- `runtime_only` validation does not fail because the main backend is intentionally absent;\n- manual boot mode remains manual after diagnostic `safe-start` unless persistence is explicitly requested;\n- clean systemd unit surface no longer depends on stale `0.32.1` metadata or undocumented `hotfix` drop-ins;\n- `pipeline validate` passes on release catalogs, including media/admin pipelines;\n- degraded staffing behavior is handled intentionally by `mvp-smoke`;\n- failed smoke checks include command, exit code, stdout/stderr/report paths;\n- docs reflect the actual operator flow;\n- a final recheck report is attached to the PR/issue;\n- requirements reconciliation has created/updated TODOs for remaining gaps.\n\n## Current local evidence summary\n\nFrom the Trixie host re-entry:\n\n- system baseline is clean: no failed units, ext4/io errors absent, NVIDIA works;\n- NF `runtime_only` safe core starts successfully;\n- install payload issues were found and locally repaired with chmod/chown;\n- `pipeline validate` currently fails on missing `media_team`;\n- `pipeline approve/advance` in smoke state is blocked by `degraded_readonly` under `degraded_selected`;\n- `pipeline validate --json` currently rejects `--json`.\n\n## Safety constraints\n\n- Do not enable heavy LLM autostart.\n- Do not raise `max_active_llms` above 1 for this release path.\n- Do not make `/opt/noemaforge` mutable runtime state.\n- Do not hide failed checks as green unless they are explicitly classified as expected skip/degraded with evidence.\n- Do not loop endlessly on repeated failures; after repeated failure, change approach or open an issue with evidence.","comments":[],"labels":[{"id":"LA_kwDOSdiUqc8AAAACjNlHzQ","name":"bug","description":"Something isn't working","color":"d73a4a"}],"number":221,"state":"OPEN","title":"Codex task: drive 0.33.0 prod-ready loop for install/re-entry, docs, recheck, requirements reconciliation, TODOs","url":"https://github.com/Sinev-Maksim/NoemaForge/issues/221"}

